      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62945,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>This is usually silent clinically and seen at surgery or on biopsy for other conditions.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T14:11:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62946,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mesothelial hyperplasia is a common incidental finding.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62947,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mesothelial hyperplasia is a reactive condition that occurs in response to pelvic inflammation, peritoneal effusion, endometriosis, and tumours {8418078; 21421699; 24901399}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62948,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62949,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It can show small nodules or coat the peritoneum {24901399}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62950,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>The hyperplastic mesothelial cells grow as small aggregates/sheets, single cells, cords, and tubulopapillary structures admixed with inflammation. An infiltrative appearance, lymphovascular invasion, enlarged nuclei, multinucleation, prominent nucleoli, scattered mitoses, and deciduoid features may be seen {21421699; 23855881; 24901399}. Cells are typically positive for desmin and negative for EMA, GLUT1, and IMP3, whereas mesothelioma shows the opposite staining pattern {26288396}. Unlike well-differentiated papillary mesothelial tumour, mesothelial hyperplasia lacks expression of L1CAM {30171198}. Unlike mesothelioma, mesothelial hyperplasia shows no loss of BAP1 by immunohistochemistry {26288396}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-21T18:39:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62951,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In cytology samples, the mesothelial cells show mild to moderate nuclear pleomorphism, multinucleation, mitotic figures, cytoplasmic vacuoles, and psammoma bodies {23858317}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62952,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mesothelial hyperplasia lacks <em>BAP1</em> mutations and homozygous deletion of <em>CDKN2A</em> (p16) by FISH {26288396}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62953,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> benign cytological features and lack of invasive growth.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> BAP1 immunohistochemistry and <em>CDKN2A</em> (p16) FISH in selected cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62954,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62955,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 155,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a benign lesion.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:19:12"
      }
    ],
